+## Invoice tax
+
+`computeInvoice(lines, { taxRatePercent, discountPercent = 0 })` from `src/tax.js` takes lines of `{ quantity, unitCents }` (a negative quantity is a credit line) and percentages with at most two decimals.
+
+- The invoice discount is `discountPercent` of the positive line nets, rounded half to even, and is split across the positive lines in proportion to their nets with the largest-remainder method (ties go to the earlier line). Credit lines get no discount.
+- Each line's tax is `taxRatePercent` of its net minus its discount, rounded half to even (symmetric for negatives).
+- It returns `{ lines, netCents, discountCents, taxCents, grossCents }`, with `{ netCents, discountCents, taxCents, grossCents }` per line. The math is exact integer arithmetic.
+
 ## Delivery
 
 `estimateDelivery(orderedAt, transitDays)` returns the expected delivery date in Istanbul time.
